From b5996b638a932843c9f443432e5762a0a26d5578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 08:17:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] drm, rendervulkan: address GBM scanout review feedback

- Rebuild the output images when drm_gbm_scanout is toggled at runtime:
  the convar now sets g_bForceOutputImageRemake, which steamcompmgr's
  output-change check picks up, instead of waiting for an unrelated
  resolution/HDR change.
- Retry with plain Vulkan allocation when a BInit that internally chose
  an external (GBM) scanout buffer fails at a later step (vkCreateImage,
  memory import, fbid creation). BInit is now a wrapper around
  BInitInternal, with the destructor factored into ReleaseResources()
  so a failed attempt can be cleaned up and retried. Also destroy the
  VkImage independently of memory ownership so failed or aliased images
  don't leak the handle.
- Create the GBM device on a dup of the KMS fd and close it in the
  device deleter, so gbm_bo_destroy from textures that outlive the
  backend on shutdown doesn't operate on a closed (or reused) fd after
  wlsession_close_kms().
- Select the dmabuf import memory type from the mask reported by
  vkGetMemoryFdPropertiesKHR intersected with the image requirements,
  as the external-memory spec requires, instead of the image
  requirements alone. Applies to all dmabuf imports, not just GBM ones.

Also guard the internal external-scanout attempt against callers that
pass their own backend fb, where a replacement buffer would not match
the fb being scanned out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ZqFjz2VRJrkstciYqbXbg
